  "skip_reason": "η-direction sibling of `fv3_sinsg_flux_xi`. Layer-A canonical drive requires the same cubed_sphere selector + metric-binding extension in ESS `discretize` (v_edge selector, per-cell `sin_pos`/`sin_neg`/`dy` resolved by `_precompute_sinsg_eta`, scalar `dt`). The η rule's algebra is the (xi, west, east) ↔ (eta, south, north) coordinate-mirror image of the ξ sibling, so once the cubed_sphere walker dispatch lands, the canonical fixture can be authored either by reflecting the ξ canonical fixture or by pinning a separate η-direction reference; the bit-equivalence content is captured under the imperative reference `compute_flux_with_sinsg_eta_arrayop` in `src/operators/wind_ops.jl`.",
